      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n\n\nFix LoRA weight loading on `attention_k_eq_v` full-attention layers (e.g. `google/gemma-4-31b-it`), where the V slice of the packed `qkv_proj` received no LoRA delta even though HF applies the `k_proj` LoRA to V.\n\nThis PR is another version of #61267, where using the existing `packed_modules_mapping` mechanism instead of introducing a new \"ad-hoc\" implicit mapping rule.\n\n## Claims\n\n\n\n- On `attention_k_eq_v` full-attention layers, the fused projection is now named `qkk_proj`, and the Gemma 4 models (`Gemma4ForCausalLM`, `Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration`, `DiffusionGemmaForConditionalGeneration`) map it as `\"qkk_proj\": [\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"k_proj\"]`. Sliding-window layers keep `qkv_proj` → `[q_proj, k_proj, v_proj]`, and KV-shared layers are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n\n\n```shell\npytest tests/lora/test_lora_manager.py -k packed_loras -v\n```\n\n```log\n...\n============================================================================== 4 passed, 38 deselected, 14 warnings in 7.54s =============================================================================\n```\n\n## Details\n\n\n\nCompared to #61267, this PR does not introduce a new dynamic attribute(`.lora_packed_modules`) at the cost of touching more model codebase.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
